-- Deferred Specifications
------------------------------------------------------------

deferred SpineRouting.route            -- see: relir-migration.allium
deferred SpineRouting.coverage         -- see: relir-migration.allium

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Open Questions
------------------------------------------------------------

open question "Which passes are ORDERED relative to each other, and who runs them? `land` must precede the bind-budget refusal, `prune` must precede replication, and `name` must run last because it alone returns a program rather than a relation. No pipeline object states this today. (docs/outstanding-work.md item 37)"

open question "The statement-text budget now has an owner for the READ route only — the routing seam refuses on the platform's own limits, which covers text as well as binds. What has no owner is the replication ceiling: the pass that multiplies plan size is meant to consult rendered size and decline, and it is unbuilt."
